        "title": "feat: add session-limit reset confetti celebration",
        "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds an opt-in **Session limit confetti** celebration that plays full-screen confetti when a provider's session usage resets, alongside the existing weekly-limit celebration.\n\n<img width=\"658\" height=\"854\" alt=\"Session limit confetti preference\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6d5c9bb6-7680-436f-bf4a-14efd7b38195\" />\n\nThe setting is **off by default**. Users explicitly enable it under Settings → Advanced → Session limit confetti.\n\n## Maintainer hardening\n\n- Resolve non-Codex session observations through the canonical `sessionQuotaWindow` seam rather than treating every approximately five-hour history lane as a session.\n- Resolve Codex through the semantic consumer projection, so session detection is stable when lanes are reordered.\n- Persist the selected source with detector state. A source change establishes a new baseline instead of generating false confetti.\n- Preserve legacy persisted detector state so upgrades can still recognize the first real reset.\n- Ignore incomplete provider samples so a temporarily missing session window cannot become a false reset.\n- Recognize z.ai's semantic five-hour session lane even when weekly and monthly windows occupy the primary and secondary slots.\n- Keep session and weekly detector state independent; existing weekly-limit behavior is unchanged.\n- Add focused coverage for Copilot fallback, arbitrary secondary-window rejection, Antigravity source changes, generic-history rejection, legacy state, Codex lane ordering, detector isolation, incomplete samples, and z.ai lane ordering.\n- Keep the preference default-off and thank @bystritskiy in the changelog.\n\n## Validation — exact head `e0a708a82`\n\n- `make check` — pass (format, lint, locale, package, signing, and documentation checks).\n- `make test` — pass; 522 selections across 44 groups.\n- `swift test --filter UsageStorePlanUtilizationTests` — 51 tests pass.\n- `swift test --filter SettingsStoreTests` — 66 tests pass.\n- Structured autoreview — clean; no accepted/actionable findings.\n- Packaged ad-hoc app — app and unstripped binary UUIDs match (`18B6B243-D306-3F39-A226-44EB770ADA02`).\n- Tart macOS VM — the exact UI baseline at `776752483` stayed running; preference value was enabled for the test; live full-screen confetti was captured. The three later commits change only reset-source state/model logic, covered above, and do not touch rendering or settings UI. The local screenshot is intentionally not uploaded by the maintainer.\n- [Exact-head CI](https://github.com/steipete/CodexBar/actions/runs/28511987151) — approved; awaiting runner availability.\n\n## Behavior\n\nThe detector posts one session-reset event on a real above-threshold → reset transition. The app reuses the existing click-through, full-screen confetti overlay; no new rendering surface or provider probe is introduced.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
